\c 42  
\ms1 BOOK 2  
\d For the Chief Musician. A contemplation by the sons of Korah.  
\q1
\v 1 \w As|strong="H1121"\w* \w the|strong="H1121"\w* deer pants \w for|strong="H1121"\w* \w the|strong="H1121"\w* water brooks,  
\q2 so my soul pants after you, God.\f + \fr 42:1 \ft The Hebrew word rendered “God” is “\+wh אֱלֹהִ֑ים\+wh*” (Elohim).\f*   
\q1
\v 2 \w My|strong="H5921"\w* \w soul|strong="H5315"\w* thirsts \w for|strong="H5921"\w* God, \w for|strong="H5921"\w* \w the|strong="H5921"\w* \w living|strong="H5315"\w* God.  
\q2 \w When|strong="H5921"\w* \w shall|strong="H5315"\w* \w I|strong="H5921"\w* come \w and|strong="H4325"\w* appear \w before|strong="H5921"\w* God?   
